1
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:49,080
And give her a teaspoon of the medicine after every meal.

2
00:00:49,080 --> 00:00:51,300
Don't worry. She'll be fine.

3
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:54,600
You're welcome. Good-bye.

4
00:00:54,600 --> 00:01:05,400
How are you?

5
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:07,300
I'm tired and hungry.

6
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:08,860
Well, Marilyn and Richard called.

7
00:01:08,860 --> 00:01:10,300
They'll be here soon, and then we'll eat.

8
00:01:10,300 --> 00:01:13,200
All right. Is...is Susan coming?

9
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:15,000
Well, she'll be here later.

10
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:16,300
She has to work late tonight.

11
00:01:16,300 --> 00:01:17,460
And what's Robbie cooking for dinner? Robbie

12
00:01:17,460 --> 00:01:20,040
It's a surprise.

13
00:01:20,040 --> 00:01:22,600
I hope it's pasta.

14
00:01:22,600 --> 00:01:28,900
Robbie, the dinner was terrific. Robbie

15
00:01:28,900 --> 00:01:30,200
Yes, it was delicious.

16
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:32,940
What's for dessert?

17
00:01:32,940 --> 00:01:34,660
Oh, I forgot dessert.

18
00:01:34,660 --> 00:01:37,240
Robbie! Robbie

19
00:01:37,240 --> 00:01:38,100
Don't worry.

20
00:01:38,100 --> 00:01:39,820
We've got lots of ice cream.

21
00:01:39,820 --> 00:01:41,600
Oh, I'd love some ice cream.

22
00:01:41,600 --> 00:01:46,300
Well, there's chocolate and coffee and a little vanilla.

23
00:01:46,300 --> 00:01:47,700
I'll have vanilla.

24
00:01:47,700 --> 00:01:49,500
Is that all right with everyone?

25
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:50,000
I'll have chocolate.

26
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:51,860
Me, too.

27
00:01:51,860 --> 00:01:54,440
Uh, one scoop of coffee

28
00:01:54,440 --> 00:01:56,500
and one scoop of chocolate for me.

29
00:01:56,500 --> 00:01:59,100
Robbie, will you help me serve? Robbie

30
00:01:59,100 --> 00:02:11,100
I keep thinking about that bag of film. Eight rolls.

31
00:02:11,100 --> 00:02:14,500
A whole day's work.

32
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:15,940
And good stuff, too.

33
00:02:15,940 --> 00:02:17,900
Don't worry, Richard.

34
00:02:17,900 --> 00:02:18,400
Somenoe will find it.

35
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:23,400
I'll get it. Hello.

36
00:02:23,400 --> 00:02:29,700
Hello.

37
00:02:29,700 --> 00:02:32,200
Does Richard Stewart live here? Richard Stewart

38
00:02:32,200 --> 00:02:34,500
Yes, he's my brother.

39
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:35,720
I'm Robbie...Robbie Stewart.

40
00:02:35,720 --> 00:02:38,500
I'm Alexandra Pappas.

41
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:38,900
How do you do?

42
00:02:38,900 --> 00:02:42,400
Your brother left his bag of film on the ferryboat.

43
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:43,600
I found it.

44
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:45,100
I'm really glad to see you.

45
00:02:45,100 --> 00:02:47,400
I mean...my brother'll be really glad to see you!

46
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:49,100
Robbie! Who is it? Robbie

47
00:02:49,100 --> 00:02:52,500
It's Richard's film! Richard

48
00:02:52,500 --> 00:02:54,900
I mean, Alexandra Pappas.

49
00:02:54,900 --> 00:02:56,500
Come in, please.

50
00:02:56,500 --> 00:03:02,500
Alexandra! Alexandra

51
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:03,700
Hello, Richard. I found your bag!

52
00:03:03,700 --> 00:03:06,700
Oh, thank you! Thank you!

53
00:03:06,700 --> 00:03:08,800
Um...Alexandra, let me introduce you.

54
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:10,200
This is my wife Marilyn.

55
00:03:10,200 --> 00:03:11,500
Richard showed me your photo. Richard

56
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:12,800
How do you do?

57
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:13,200
Oh yes.

58
00:03:13,200 --> 00:03:14,300
Richard told us all about you. Richard

59
00:03:14,300 --> 00:03:16,300
It's nice to meet you.

60
00:03:16,300 --> 00:03:18,100
And this is my mother, Ellen Stewart.

61
00:03:18,100 --> 00:03:18,800
How do you do?

62
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:20,200
And my father, Dr. Philip Stewart.

63
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:22,200
Nice to meet you, Alexandra.

64
00:03:22,200 --> 00:03:23,000
And...ah...you met Robbie.

65
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:25,900
Yes. And you must be Susan. Hi.

66
00:03:25,900 --> 00:03:27,320
Hi. Welcome.

67
00:03:27,320 --> 00:03:29,040
I'm so glad you found the bag

68
00:03:29,040 --> 00:03:31,620
and took the time and trouble to return it.

69
00:03:31,620 --> 00:03:32,480
Oh, it was no trouble.

70
00:03:32,480 --> 00:03:34,500
I just took the wrong train.

71
00:03:34,500 --> 00:03:35,700
Would you like something to eat?

72
00:03:35,700 --> 00:03:36,400
Thank you, no.

73
00:03:36,400 --> 00:03:38,200
I'm late for dinner at my house.

74
00:03:38,200 --> 00:03:39,360
I really have to go.

75
00:03:39,360 --> 00:03:41,500
Would you like to call home?

76
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:41,900
I'd appreciate that.

77
00:03:41,900 --> 00:03:43,900
Please, use the phone.

78
00:03:43,900 --> 00:03:45,380
Thanks. Excuse me.

79
00:03:45,380 --> 00:03:48,820
Alexandra's a high-school exchange student from Greece. Alexandra

80
00:03:48,820 --> 00:03:49,400
Where does she live?

81
00:03:49,400 --> 00:03:51,400
With a family in the Bronx.

82
00:03:51,400 --> 00:03:53,000
Oh, that's not too far from here!

83
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,840
Take it easy, Robbie.

84
00:03:54,840 --> 00:03:57,000
Thank you.

85
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:58,280
I can only stay a few minutes.

86
00:03:58,280 --> 00:04:00,860
Have some iced tea.

87
00:04:00,860 --> 00:04:02,700
Thanks, Mrs. Stewart.

88
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:04,800
Please sit down, Alexandra.

89
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:13,200
So, you're an exchange student.

90
00:04:13,200 --> 00:04:13,760
Where do you go to school?

91
00:04:13,760 --> 00:04:16,000
At the Bronx High School of Science.

92
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:18,300
Oh, that's a very good school.

93
00:04:18,300 --> 00:04:19,900
What are your favorite subjects?

94
00:04:19,900 --> 00:04:21,200
Biology and mathematics.

95
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:23,700
Richard tells me you're a doctor. Richard

96
00:04:23,700 --> 00:04:25,000
Yes, a pediatrician.

97
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:26,700
And what does your father do?

98
00:04:26,700 --> 00:04:29,700
He's a lawyer, in Thessaloniki.

99
00:04:29,700 --> 00:04:29,900
Would you like some pasta?

100
00:04:29,700 --> 00:04:31,820
I made it myself.

101
00:04:31,820 --> 00:04:33,100
It might be a little cold.

102
00:04:33,100 --> 00:04:36,900
Thanks, no. I do have to go.

103
00:04:36,900 --> 00:04:38,900
It was nice meeting you all.

104
00:04:38,900 --> 00:04:40,500
Well, maybe you'll come for lunch some Sunday,

105
00:04:40,500 --> 00:04:42,600
so we can really thank you

106
00:04:42,600 --> 00:04:42,800
for bringing Richard's bag back.

107
00:04:42,600 --> 00:04:43,860
Maybe.

108
00:04:43,860 --> 00:04:44,720
You're welcome anytime.

109
00:04:44,720 --> 00:04:47,700
Good-bye.

110
00:04:47,700 --> 00:04:53,400
Can I drive you home?

111
00:04:53,400 --> 00:04:54,180
No, thanks.

112
00:04:54,180 --> 00:04:55,500
The train is just up the street.

113
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:56,000
It won't take me long at all.

114
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:58,500
Well, you really saved the day for me, Alexandra.

115
00:04:58,500 --> 00:04:59,700
Bye.

116
00:04:59,700 --> 00:05:01,060
Bye-bye.

117
00:05:01,060 --> 00:05:01,920
Good night.

118
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:11,300
She's a smart young lady, and very nice.

119
00:05:11,300 --> 00:05:15,200
Very! Hey, she forgot her bag!

120
00:05:15,200 --> 00:05:17,300
I guess we'll be seeing Alexandra again.

121
00:05:17,300 --> 00:05:20,300
Right, Robbie?
